# Convert

Value conversions, written in pure LOGOS and compiled through every execution tier.
Auto-imported on first reference.

## Note
Renders an integer as its decimal text via string interpolation.

## To numText (n: Int) -> Text:
    Return "{n}".

## Note
Returns the byte code of the first byte of text `s`.

## To ord (s: Text) -> Int:
    Return item 1 of text_bytes(s).

## Note
Renders integer `n` in the given radix `base`, using digits `0`-`9` then lowercase letters for values 10 and up.

## To toBase (n: Int) and (base: Int) -> Text:
    If n is equal to 0:
        Return "0".
    Let mutable m be n.
    Let digits be a new Seq of Int.
    While m is greater than 0:
        Let d be m % base.
        Let mutable code be 48 + d.
        If d is at least 10:
            Set code to 97 + (d - 10).
        Push code to digits.
        Set m to m / base.
    Let out be a new Seq of Int.
    Let k be length of digits.
    Let mutable i be k.
    While i is at least 1:
        Push item i of digits to out.
        Set i to i - 1.
    Return text_from_bytes(out).

## Note
Renders integer `n` in base 2 by delegating to `toBase`.

## To toBinary (n: Int) -> Text:
    Return toBase(n, 2).

## Note
Renders integer `n` in base 16 by delegating to `toBase`.

## To toHexInt (n: Int) -> Text:
    Return toBase(n, 16).

## Note
Renders integer `n` in base 8 by delegating to `toBase`.

## To toOct (n: Int) -> Text:
    Return toBase(n, 8).

## Note
Renders a boolean as the text `"true"` or `"false"`.

## To formatBool (b: Bool) -> Text:
    If b:
        Return "true".
    Return "false".

## Note
Parses truthy text — `"1"`, `"t"`, `"T"`, `"true"`, `"True"`, or `"TRUE"` yield true; anything else is false.

## To parseBool (s: Text) -> Bool:
    If s is equal to "1":
        Return true.
    If s is equal to "t":
        Return true.
    If s is equal to "T":
        Return true.
    If s is equal to "true":
        Return true.
    If s is equal to "True":
        Return true.
    If s is equal to "TRUE":
        Return true.
    Return false.

## Note
Wraps `s` in double quotes, escaping `"`, `\`, newline (as `\n`), and tab (as `\t`).

## To quoteText (s: Text) -> Text:
    Let sb be text_bytes(s).
    Let out be a new Seq of Int.
    Push 34 to out.
    Repeat for c in sb:
        If c is equal to 34:
            Push 92 to out.
            Push 34 to out.
        Otherwise:
            If c is equal to 92:
                Push 92 to out.
                Push 92 to out.
            Otherwise:
                If c is equal to 10:
                    Push 92 to out.
                    Push 110 to out.
                Otherwise:
                    If c is equal to 9:
                        Push 92 to out.
                        Push 116 to out.
                    Otherwise:
                        Push c to out.
    Push 34 to out.
    Return text_from_bytes(out).

## Note
Reports whether `s` can be raw-backquoted: false if it contains a backtick, DEL (127), or any control byte below 32 other than tab (9).

## To canBackquote (s: Text) -> Bool:
    Let sb be text_bytes(s).
    Let mutable ok be true.
    Repeat for c in sb:
        If c is equal to 96:
            Set ok to false.
        If c is equal to 127:
            Set ok to false.
        If c is less than 32:
            If c is greater than 9:
                Set ok to false.
            Otherwise:
                If c is less than 9:
                    Set ok to false.
    Return ok.

## Note
Parses `s` as an integer, clamping any negative result to 0.

## To parseUint (s: Text) -> Int:
    Let n be parseInt(s).
    If n is less than 0:
        Return 0.
    Return n.

## Note
Renders an integer as its decimal text via string interpolation.

## To formatUint (n: Int) -> Text:
    Return "{n}".

## Note
Converts an integer to a Real via the Int-times-Real coercion — a direct `n as f64` cast, not a decimal-text round-trip through `parseFloat`.

## To toReal (n: Int) -> Real:
    Return n + 0.0.

## Note
Appends the decimal text of integer `n` to `prefix`.

## To appendInt (prefix: Text) and (n: Int) -> Text:
    Return prefix combined with "{n}".

## Note
Appends the decimal text of integer `n` to `prefix`.

## To appendUint (prefix: Text) and (n: Int) -> Text:
    Return prefix combined with "{n}".

## Note
Appends the formatted boolean (`"true"`/`"false"`) to `prefix`.

## To appendBool (prefix: Text) and (b: Bool) -> Text:
    Return prefix combined with formatBool(b).

## Note
Appends the double-quoted, escaped form of `s` (via `quoteText`) to `prefix`.

## To appendQuote (prefix: Text) and (s: Text) -> Text:
    Return prefix combined with quoteText(s).

## Note
Wraps the character for code `c` (via `chr`) in single quotes.

## To quoteRune (c: Int) -> Text:
    Return "'" combined with chr(c) combined with "'".

## Note
Appends the single-quoted character for code `c` (via `quoteRune`) to `prefix`.

## To appendQuoteRune (prefix: Text) and (c: Int) -> Text:
    Return prefix combined with quoteRune(c).
